On Sat, Jun 18, 2011 at 5:59 PM, Alex Rozenshteyn <rpglover64@gmail.com> wrote:
> To be fair, the number of lojban utterances is countable...

It depends on what you mean by utterance. If I say "coi" and you say
"coi", do those count as two utterances or as one and the same?

The number of utterance types is countable, the number of potential
utterance tokens is uncountable, the number of actual utterance tokens
is probably not just countable but finite.

But we were comparing ka-expressions and properties, so I'm not sure I
see how the number of utterances comes in. the number of ka-expression
types is countable, and the number of properties is uncountable.

